# pagehub-benchmarks — environment.  Copy to .env (gitignored) and edit.

# --- harness: Claude Code ---------------------------------------------------
# Benchmark runs use the `claude` CLI's existing logged-in auth (a Claude
# subscription — flat-rate, not metered API billing). The adapter explicitly
# UNSETS ANTHROPIC_API_KEY in the subprocess so a stray key can't divert the
# run onto API billing — don't set one here. If `claude -p` says "not logged
# in", run `claude login`. (cost_usd in results is a *computed* figure:
# tokens x pricing.yaml = "what this would cost at API rates".)

# Max seconds for one `claude` invocation (one attempt). Default 3600.
# CLAUDE_BUILD_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=3600

# --- harness: Codex CLI (OpenAI) ----------------------------------------------
# Runs use the `codex` CLI's stored ChatGPT-subscription login (`codex login`,
# or `codex login --device-auth` on a headless box). The adapter UNSETS
# CODEX_API_KEY, CODEX_ACCESS_TOKEN and OPENAI_API_KEY in the subprocess and
# refuses to run unless `codex login status` reports "Logged in using ChatGPT"
# — an API-key login would silently move the run onto metered billing. Don't
# set any of those here. CODEX_HOME is honoured (default ~/.codex).

# Max seconds for one `codex exec` leg (a retried attempt is several legs).
# Default 3600.
# CODEX_BUILD_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=3600

# How many times a *dead* turn (codex answered, but the model never ran: auth
# or transport failure, a rejected prompt) is retried, 5 s apart, before the
# run fails loudly. Default 2. Turns in which the model did work and then
# failed are never retried — they are recorded as attempt failures.
# CODEX_DEAD_TURN_RETRIES=2

# NOTE: Claude Code's agent sees everything your ~/.bashrc exports (it runs
# unsandboxed with your HOME). The codex adapter gives its agent a throwaway
# HOME under ~/.cache/pagehub-benchmarks/codex-homes (so ~/.bashrc is not
# sourced) and filters secret-named inherited variables. Keeping secrets out
# of the runner's shell profile, or benchmarking under a dedicated user, is
# still the right hygiene. XDG_CACHE_HOME moves that directory; it must not
# be under /tmp or $TMPDIR (the codex sandbox makes those writable).

# --- grader: pagehub-evals --------------------------------------------------
# Where the pagehub-evals repo is checked out (the grader resolves a
# benchmark's grader.fixture_bundle path relative to this). Default:
# ~/github/pagehub-io/pagehub-evals
# PAGEHUB_EVALS_REPO=~/github/pagehub-io/pagehub-evals

# Operator bearer token for pagehub-evals (fixture import + resource listing
# are operator-only). If unset, a dev HS256 token is minted from the values
# below — only works against a dev pagehub-evals (docker-compose defaults).
# PAGEHUB_EVALS_TOKEN=eyJ...
# PAGEHUB_EVALS_JWT_SIGNING_KEY=dev-kid:local-dev-jwt-signing-key-DO-NOT-USE-IN-PROD
# PAGEHUB_EVALS_JWT_ISSUER=http://localhost:8080
# PAGEHUB_EVALS_OPERATOR_EMAIL=support@pagehub.io
